231
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:23,480
License is a weird word, but you've got to use it because it starts with an L, and that's

232
00:15:23,480 --> 00:15:23,860
what we do.

233
00:15:23,860 --> 00:15:26,120
So legalism, right?

234
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,820
We try and legislate the behavior out of our lives.

235
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:33,020
We try and say, I'm never going to do this thing again, so I'm going to create this box

236
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:33,600
around my life.

237
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,000
I'm going to force myself to do these things that I don't want to do.

238
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,820
We try and legislate it.

239
00:15:37,820 --> 00:15:39,860
We try and create this legalistic mindset.

240
00:15:39,860 --> 00:15:43,880
And for any of us that have tried it, it works for a little bit.

241
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:46,560
And then sometimes it makes it worse.

242
00:15:46,560 --> 00:15:52,300
Legalism falls short of God's design for the Christian life.

243
00:15:52,300 --> 00:15:58,160
Paul says in Galatians earlier in the book, he says, if righteousness comes through the law,

244
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:02,920
if righteousness comes from our being able to do it, being able to create a law, a structure

245
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:06,300
around our lives, then Christ died for no purpose.

246
00:16:06,300 --> 00:16:12,420
Since legalism is wasting the sacrificial death of Jesus on your behalf.

247
00:16:12,420 --> 00:16:13,720
Legalism is not the answer.

248
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:16,620
The second thing that we often turn to is license.

249
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:22,240
We start to redefine what is right and wrong, and we convince ourselves that God doesn't care

250
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:28,160
about our behavior, that God just wants to keep forgiving us and abounding us with more

251
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:28,740
and more grace.

252
00:16:28,740 --> 00:16:32,060
And he doesn't care if we try and be obedient or we try and grow in our faith.

253
00:16:32,060 --> 00:16:32,780
He doesn't care.

254
00:16:32,780 --> 00:16:36,660
This is the struggle that Paul wrestles with in Romans.

255
00:16:36,660 --> 00:16:41,340
He says the Romans, he kind of asks this hypothetical question that he hears from people.

256
00:16:41,340 --> 00:16:46,600
They say, shouldn't we just keep on sinning so that grace, so that God can show us more

257
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,140
and more of his wonderful grace.

258
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:53,500
So if we tried legalism and it failed, then oftentimes we say, I'm just, I'm a sinner.

259
00:16:53,500 --> 00:16:54,880
I'm broken.

260
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:56,260
I'm never going to get it right.

261
00:16:56,260 --> 00:16:59,640
So I'm just going to keep on sinning more and more because God loves me and his grace

262
00:16:59,640 --> 00:17:01,060
is wonderful and awesome.

263
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:06,380
Now, in both of these realities, there's truth, right?

264
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:13,400
Like, God cares about our behavior and we should participate in this process of being made like

265
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:16,440
Jesus, but it can't happen to the extent of legalism.

266
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:23,220
And at the same time, like, God is abounding in grace and love and we cannot out sin the forgiveness

267
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:24,360
and grace of Jesus.

268
00:17:24,360 --> 00:17:29,000
But both of these solutions fall short.

269
00:17:29,860 --> 00:17:35,340
They fall short of God's design for our lives and they rob us of the abundant life that Jesus

270
00:17:35,340 --> 00:17:37,600
died to purchase.

271
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:42,220
So if legalism and license aren't the answer, then how do we solve this tension?

272
00:17:42,220 --> 00:17:47,740
Well, I think that's why Paul introduces this illustration of fruit of the Spirit.

273
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:53,180
I think this illustration opens up our minds to how we can participate with God in the process.

274
00:17:53,500 --> 00:17:59,640
In verse 19, he says, when you follow the desires of your sinful nature, the results are very

275
00:17:59,640 --> 00:18:00,040
clear.

276
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:03,000
Sexual immorality, impurity, lustful pleasures.

277
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
This is the part we don't put on the coffee mug.

278
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:06,600
So if you're not familiar with it, that's why.

279
00:18:06,600 --> 00:18:15,120
Idolatry, sorcery, hostility, quarreling, jealousy, outbursts of anger, selfish ambition,

280
00:18:15,120 --> 00:18:18,640
dissension, division, envy, drunkenness, wild parties.

281
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:20,540
Again, this would not look good on a t-shirt.

282
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:26,860
And other sins like these, let me tell you again, as I have before, that anyone living

283
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:30,040
that sort of life will not inherit the kingdom of God.

284
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:35,240
But the Holy Spirit, who does it?

285
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,160
Do you do it?

286
00:18:36,160 --> 00:18:37,160
Or does the Holy Spirit do it?

287
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:41,780
The Holy Spirit produces this kind of fruit in your life.

288
00:18:41,780 --> 00:18:47,920
Love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control.

289
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:52,660
There is no law against such things.

290
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:58,720
So there are multiple illustrations in the New Testament that Paul and other writers use

291
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:03,740
to try and wrestle with this tension of you don't do what you want to do, like you want

292
00:19:03,740 --> 00:19:05,560
to obey God and you try and you fail.

293
00:19:05,560 --> 00:19:08,080
And then you do what you don't want to do.

294
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:10,200
You naturally just sin and sin and sin.

295
00:19:10,760 --> 00:19:15,700
And the writers of the New Testament use multiple illustrations, things like you are born again.

296
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:19,040
You've been adopted into a new family.

297
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:21,160
You have been crucified with Christ, right?

298
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:22,440
You're familiar with this language.

299
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,680
You've died.

300
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:24,440
You've been buried.

301
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:26,840
And you've been brought to new life.

302
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:31,800
And the goal is to show, like, hey, this old sinful nature in you has been put to death

303
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:34,280
and you've been adopted into a new family.

304
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:37,660
The family code is no longer that of sin and selfishness.

305
00:19:37,660 --> 00:19:40,540
The family code is that of what Jesus modeled for us.

306
00:19:40,540 --> 00:19:43,260
And all of these illustrations are helpful and good.

307
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:50,880
But I personally think that this illustration of fruit does the best job at reconciling how

308
00:19:50,880 --> 00:19:54,300
the individual Christian participates in this process.

309
00:19:54,300 --> 00:20:00,760
See, when Marissa and I moved out here, we bought an old house with a couple acres.

310
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:09,460
And ever since then, I've had this desire to use the land, to grow a garden, to plant things,

311
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:12,080
to get animals, to do all of the things.

312
00:20:13,220 --> 00:20:16,180
And it's been, what, over a year now?

313
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,180
I haven't done any.

314
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:19,400
I haven't.

315
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:28,500
And the reason that I haven't, I really like the idea of eating off of the land that God

316
00:20:28,500 --> 00:20:29,580
has provided for us.

317
00:20:29,580 --> 00:20:30,720
But here's why I haven't.

318
00:20:30,720 --> 00:20:31,880
Because I know.

319
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:41,100
I know the moment that I till up a piece of ground that I am starting a lifelong war against

320
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,400
the effects of the curse.

321
00:20:43,100 --> 00:20:43,280
Right?

322
00:20:43,280 --> 00:20:45,420
Like, we get this in Genesis chapter 3.

323
00:20:45,420 --> 00:20:50,000
Like, God says, part of the fall is like, it's hard to produce things.

324
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,460
Work is hard.

325
00:20:51,460 --> 00:20:53,940
Taking care of the land is difficult.

326
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:59,100
And I know the moment that I till up the land, there's going to be animals that come out of

327
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:02,160
nowhere to try and eat the fruit that I'm trying to harvest.

328
00:21:02,160 --> 00:21:07,040
There's going to be weather things that I can't predict or don't know about.

329
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:10,960
There's going to be weeds that start to grow up around the plant that I'm trying to harvest.

330
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:17,580
There's going to be all of this outside forces at work to keep the garden from producing fruit.

331
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:22,400
The second thing is I personally know nothing about plants.

332
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:26,780
Like, it's embarrassing how much I don't know about plants.

333
00:21:26,780 --> 00:21:31,860
And I know that if I'm going to garden, I should probably know a few things about the plants in the garden.

334
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:36,640
I should know the difference between the weed and the plant because that could be problematic, right?

335
00:21:36,640 --> 00:21:42,100
And so, I haven't gotten over these lame excuses.

336
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:48,460
But if I did, if I got over these lame excuses, started a garden, and then one day in the next few months

337
00:21:48,460 --> 00:21:53,100
was able to harvest a cucumber or two and slice it up and put it in my salad,

338
00:21:53,100 --> 00:21:58,140
would it make sense for me to sit back, take a bite of that cucumber, and say,

339
00:21:58,140 --> 00:22:02,720
man, I am so proud that I grew this cucumber?

340
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:05,180
Would that make sense?

341
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:10,100
No, it wouldn't because I didn't grow the cucumber.

342
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,960
I cannot grow a cucumber.

343
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:17,280
Nothing, like, growing a cucumber takes so many things outside of my control.

344
00:22:17,280 --> 00:22:21,000
Sunlight, photosynthesis, like, soil that I didn't create.

345
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:27,420
There's so many aspects of the cucumber coming to life out of the soil that God's in charge of

346
00:22:27,420 --> 00:22:29,180
that I have no control over.

347
00:22:29,180 --> 00:22:35,820
But what I can do and pretty much have to do if I want this garden to produce fruit

348
00:22:35,820 --> 00:22:39,040
is I have to work to create a hospitable environment.

349
00:22:40,100 --> 00:22:44,760
For God's work to happen in the garden.

350
00:22:44,760 --> 00:22:51,520
And if you're here and you're a follower of Jesus, God has taken up residence in your life.

351
00:22:51,520 --> 00:22:54,420
The Scriptures say the Holy Spirit has come into your life.

352
00:22:54,420 --> 00:23:00,780
Essentially what Paul is saying is God has shown up in your life and he has planted a garden on your property.

353
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:08,180
God has planted a garden on your property and his goal, his purpose, is to create the fruit of the Spirit in your life.

354
00:23:08,180 --> 00:23:12,900
God has planted a garden with all of these aspects of the character of Jesus in your life.

355
00:23:12,900 --> 00:23:21,900
His goal is to conform you into the image of Jesus, which is love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness,

356
00:23:22,140 --> 00:23:24,140
faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control.

357
00:23:24,140 --> 00:23:28,740
This is the goal of God in the life of a believer.

358
00:23:28,740 --> 00:23:36,340
But the moment he does that, stuff comes out.

359
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:40,260
Like your own sinful flesh comes out.

360
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:46,320
The enemy at work outside of your life wants to keep that fruit from being produced in your life.

361
00:23:46,380 --> 00:23:48,520
And you can't do anything to produce the fruit.

362
00:23:48,520 --> 00:23:49,580
God did it all.

363
00:23:49,580 --> 00:23:59,820
But what you can do is work to create a hospitable environment for the Holy Spirit to produce this fruit in your life.

364
00:23:59,820 --> 00:24:01,720
This is your responsibility.

365
00:24:01,720 --> 00:24:05,980
This is how this tension works out.

366
00:24:05,980 --> 00:24:09,160
God produces fruit, but you can create a hospitable environment.

367
00:24:09,160 --> 00:24:09,960
How do we do that?

368
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:10,900
What does that look like?

369
00:24:12,540 --> 00:24:18,940
Well, number one, you identify the outside influences that want to infringe on the Spirit producing the fruit in your life.

370
00:24:18,940 --> 00:24:26,620
And Paul gives us a list here of some culturally relevant sins.

371
00:24:26,620 --> 00:24:34,360
You know, Paul's reacting specifically to sins that he knows are true in the church of Galatia.

372
00:24:34,520 --> 00:24:44,340
And so I'm not going to spend a whole ton of time diving into the specifics of the outside forces that are at work trying to keep the Holy Spirit from producing fruit in the lives of the Galatians.

373
00:24:44,340 --> 00:24:53,700
But I do think this list of sins falls into a pretty nice category of sins that we still wrestle with to this day.

374
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:58,660
All of this list of sins, they fall into like three categories.

375
00:24:58,660 --> 00:25:03,080
There's sexual sin, there's spiritual sin, and there's relational sin.

376
00:25:03,080 --> 00:25:07,300
And these categories still work pretty nicely for where we're at today.

377
00:25:07,300 --> 00:25:08,200
It might look differently.

378
00:25:08,200 --> 00:25:12,500
Like sorcery probably isn't a sin that many of us in the room are struggling with.

379
00:25:12,500 --> 00:25:20,460
But idolatry, like worshiping things that aren't God, is a spiritual sin that you and I still struggle with.

380
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:33,600
Because prostitution might not be a sin that you and I struggle with, but there is sexual sins that we struggle with, selfishness in our lives.

381
00:25:33,600 --> 00:25:39,380
And I think in each one of these areas of sin, the driving, motivating thing behind it is selfishness.

382
00:25:39,380 --> 00:25:45,520
We treat our sexuality in such a way that benefits us, and we don't care how it impacts those around us.

383
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:50,080
We treat our spiritual lives very inwardly.

384
00:25:50,140 --> 00:25:56,120
We only care about our own spiritual lives and how it affects us, and we don't think about how the implications are on other people.

385
00:25:56,120 --> 00:26:02,500
Relationally, the longest part of this list, Paul lists like 20 sins and like 16 of them are relational.

386
00:26:02,500 --> 00:26:06,760
He cares about how we treat our neighbors, right?

387
00:26:08,620 --> 00:26:19,160
And so often, the predators that come out that try and keep us, that try and keep the Holy Spirit from producing the fruit in our lives,

388
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:22,540
is this selfish desire.

389
00:26:22,540 --> 00:26:26,900
Selfish desire to do what we want to do how we want to do it.

390
00:26:26,980 --> 00:26:32,820
And Paul says, identify the areas of your life that are infringing on the Holy Spirit producing fruit.

391
00:26:32,820 --> 00:26:34,560
And here's what I can't do.

392
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:39,580
I can't go through this list and like point at each one of you and tell you, for you, what it is for you.

393
00:26:39,580 --> 00:26:46,740
But what I can do is I can invite you to spend this next week praying, seeking.

394
00:26:46,740 --> 00:26:52,660
Maybe the Holy Spirit, even now, as you're like, you know, you know which one of those things on the list is your main struggle at the moment.

395
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:55,440
And this is why it's a lifelong process, right?

396
00:26:55,440 --> 00:26:59,260
Because what you struggled with 10 years ago is probably different than what you struggle with right now.

397
00:26:59,260 --> 00:27:07,500
And so you're invited into this lifelong process of asking God, what are the things, what are the outside sins and influences in my life

398
00:27:07,500 --> 00:27:14,460
that are keeping me from being a hospitable environment for the Holy Spirit to produce fruit in my life?

399
00:27:14,460 --> 00:27:17,100
This is the question I'd love for us to wrestle with this week.

400
00:27:17,100 --> 00:27:22,940
What attitudes and actions are getting in the way of the Spirit producing fruit in my life?

401
00:27:23,440 --> 00:27:33,400
Essentially, the works of the flesh, they flow out of our selfishness, and the fruit of the Spirit is produced from the selflessness that we have seen demonstrated in Jesus.

402
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:36,480
So what attitudes and actions are getting in the way?

403
00:27:36,480 --> 00:27:48,460
The second thing that you would do, if you wanted to have the fruit of the Spirit produced in your life, is you take a look for outside influences that are keeping fruit from growing.

404
00:27:48,460 --> 00:27:53,920
And then you would get to know the fruit, both intellectually and experientially, right?

405
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:55,720
Like I said, I don't know anything about plants.

406
00:27:55,720 --> 00:27:58,560
So me harvesting plants, that would be a problem.

407
00:27:58,560 --> 00:28:01,760
I would harvest weeds and not harvest plants.

408
00:28:01,820 --> 00:28:04,920
And so I would have to get to know the plants.

409
00:28:04,920 --> 00:28:12,400
And like I said, this list is a clear, distinctive list of the holistic character of Jesus.

410
00:28:12,400 --> 00:28:16,980
And so the invitation that Paul is giving you here is get to know Jesus.

411
00:28:16,980 --> 00:28:22,980
Get to know what he's like, how he interacts with his neighbors and his enemies,

412
00:28:22,980 --> 00:28:28,540
how he responds when sin is present in his cultural day.

413
00:28:28,660 --> 00:28:29,800
Get to know Jesus.

414
00:28:29,800 --> 00:28:37,880
And then ask yourself daily, what would Jesus do if he were me in this situation in my life?

415
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:42,260
Notice how I said intellectually and experientially.

416
00:28:42,260 --> 00:28:51,400
Again, if I read a bunch of books about plants and had pictures, like I would have more information and it would be helpful.

417
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:59,500
But then you get in the garden and do the work and you'll experience some things that you wouldn't see in a textbook.

418
00:28:59,500 --> 00:29:04,540
And so get to know Jesus, both intellectually and experientially.

419
00:29:04,540 --> 00:29:08,420
Like go out and serve the poor and the powerless, the widow and the orphan.

420
00:29:08,420 --> 00:29:10,120
Do the things that Jesus did.

421
00:29:10,120 --> 00:29:13,200
Experience life the way that Jesus experienced it.

422
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:14,040
Read the Gospels.

423
00:29:14,040 --> 00:29:14,440
Pray.

424
00:29:14,440 --> 00:29:14,880
Worship.

425
00:29:14,880 --> 00:29:15,440
Rest.

426
00:29:15,440 --> 00:29:17,640
Live in community with other Christ followers.

427
00:29:17,640 --> 00:29:18,560
Serve the poor.

428
00:29:21,400 --> 00:29:31,800
So the second question I'd love for us to wrestle with this week is what attitudes and actions can I add into my life that will help create a hospitable environment for the spirit to produce fruit in my life?

429
00:29:31,800 --> 00:29:41,460
See how this kind of wrestles with legalism and license and puts it into a box that at least helps our earthly minds understand.

430
00:29:41,460 --> 00:29:42,980
Again, like you don't produce the fruit.

431
00:29:42,980 --> 00:29:43,960
You can't do it.

432
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:51,680
But you can get rid of things that don't help the environment produce fruit.

433
00:29:51,680 --> 00:29:59,560
And you can add things into your life that help the Holy Spirit, that create an environment for the Holy Spirit to produce fruit in your life.

434
00:29:59,560 --> 00:30:04,140
So this leads me to a couple of questions for the skeptics.

435
00:30:04,140 --> 00:30:07,860
I like to address the skeptic in the room because I know there's some of you in here and that's a good thing.

436
00:30:08,060 --> 00:30:10,760
We want people who are wrestling with these truths.

437
00:30:10,760 --> 00:30:16,380
So you might be thinking here, okay, will the spirit produce fruit in my life if I don't participate?

438
00:30:16,380 --> 00:30:23,500
Well, if you're in here and you've placed your faith and trust in Jesus, yes.

439
00:30:23,500 --> 00:30:27,140
Our salvation is not dependent on our works.

440
00:30:27,140 --> 00:30:31,880
If you've placed your trust and allegiance in Jesus alone, the spirit of God dwells in you.

441
00:30:31,880 --> 00:30:33,340
He has planted a garden.

442
00:30:33,440 --> 00:30:39,820
He's put the seeds of love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control in your life.

443
00:30:39,820 --> 00:30:51,240
However, this process is a lot more meaningful and beneficial and fruitful if you participate daily and regularly.

444
00:30:53,660 --> 00:30:55,300
I grew up in West Virginia.

445
00:30:55,300 --> 00:30:57,300
Don't hold this against me.

446
00:30:57,300 --> 00:31:00,520
No, it's just over the border.

447
00:31:00,520 --> 00:31:05,020
And us Virginians, let's be honest, we pretend like we're different.

448
00:31:05,020 --> 00:31:06,100
We're not that much different.

449
00:31:06,100 --> 00:31:09,140
Frederick County and Berkeley County are pretty similar.

450
00:31:09,140 --> 00:31:11,220
I'm just saying, I grew up in Berkeley County.

451
00:31:11,220 --> 00:31:12,240
I live in Frederick County.

452
00:31:13,220 --> 00:31:15,040
I just, I made a lot of enemies there.

453
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,480
But, anyway.

454
00:31:16,480 --> 00:31:18,720
No, I grew up in West Virginia.

455
00:31:18,720 --> 00:31:22,260
And my parents still live in the home that I grew up in today.

456
00:31:22,260 --> 00:31:33,060
And I had these neighbors for a while that, they pretty, they pretty much live into the stereotype that you think of when you think of West Virginia.

457
00:31:33,060 --> 00:31:36,340
And I remember a couple summers, they didn't mow their grass at all.

458
00:31:36,340 --> 00:31:38,880
Not once.

459
00:31:40,460 --> 00:31:46,580
And what happened, which is incredible, is a stalk of corn grew up in their backyard.

460
00:31:46,580 --> 00:31:48,820
Like, my dad's laughing.

461
00:31:48,820 --> 00:31:49,320
He remembers.

462
00:31:49,320 --> 00:31:50,420
I went to their yard.

463
00:31:50,420 --> 00:31:55,000
I picked up, like, literally an ear of corn out of their yard that they did not plant.

464
00:31:55,000 --> 00:32:02,980
Like, essentially what had happened, I guess, is a bird flew over their yard and pooped out a corn seed or something.

465
00:32:02,980 --> 00:32:05,700
Again, I don't know plants, so if I'm explaining this wrong.

466
00:32:05,700 --> 00:32:07,520
But they did nothing.

467
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:13,960
And somehow, like, fruit was still produced on their land.

468
00:32:13,960 --> 00:32:17,120
And maybe you're here.

469
00:32:17,120 --> 00:32:21,900
Maybe you're here and you've been neglecting the work of the Spirit in your life.

470
00:32:21,900 --> 00:32:26,240
For a couple of days or a couple of weeks.

471
00:32:26,240 --> 00:32:28,080
Maybe a couple of months.

472
00:32:28,080 --> 00:32:28,960
Maybe years.

473
00:32:28,960 --> 00:32:33,160
Maybe you haven't thought about your commitment to Jesus in forever.

474
00:32:35,800 --> 00:32:42,920
What I know to be true is the Holy Spirit is still present in your life and still wants to produce this type of fruit in your life.

475
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:51,560
He still wants you to put to death the works of the flesh and to allow him to produce the Holy Spirit's fruit in your life.

476
00:32:55,800 --> 00:33:08,200
So, I just want to encourage you to consider the ways in which you might have allowed the environment of your heart in your life to be grown up with sinfulness and selfishness.

477
00:33:08,440 --> 00:33:11,680
Maybe you've ignored the Holy Spirit's work in your life.

478
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:14,260
He's still present and wants to do a work in your life.

479
00:33:14,260 --> 00:33:19,540
And today can be a day that you can decide, I'm going to get back in the garden.

480
00:33:19,540 --> 00:33:23,240
It's a lifelong process that we've been invited to.

481
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:24,860
And we don't produce the fruits.

482
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:29,740
We just create the environment where the fruit is produced.

483
00:33:29,740 --> 00:33:35,000
We work to partner with the Holy Spirit's work in our life.

484
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:38,100
So, what might need to be taken away?

485
00:33:38,100 --> 00:33:39,460
What might need to be added?

486
00:33:39,460 --> 00:33:45,880
Not out of legalism, but out of this process of participation with God and what he wants to do in your life.

487
00:33:47,780 --> 00:33:56,800
Second question that I hear skeptics wrestling with, and this is one that I wrestled with growing up, is, okay, so does that mean people who aren't followers of Jesus can't produce this kind of fruit?

488
00:33:56,800 --> 00:34:00,140
And again, the answer is complicated.

489
00:34:00,140 --> 00:34:02,800
I would say, yes, but not completely.

490
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:06,000
See, I've heard this text misused a lot in my life.

491
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:10,760
I was taught by preachers that unbelievers can't be loving or joyful or patient or kind.

492
00:34:10,760 --> 00:34:13,780
People who don't follow Jesus can't be any of these things.

493
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:26,080
And you and I probably through experience know that in many cases, people who aren't followers of Jesus are often far more loving than followers of Jesus, far more patient or kind.

494
00:34:26,080 --> 00:34:42,220
But I would say that they can't have all of it to the extent that the Holy Spirit wants to produce because, again, notice this is something that I want to point out.

495
00:34:43,200 --> 00:34:45,000
I was probably going to point it out earlier, but I didn't.

496
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:53,640
The results of the flesh, notice it's plural, and notice the fruit of the Spirit is singular.

497
00:34:53,640 --> 00:34:56,060
Because this is a package deal.

498
00:34:56,060 --> 00:34:59,100
We don't get to pick and choose which ones come more naturally to us.

499
00:34:59,100 --> 00:35:03,080
Like, some of you in here, like, God's just giving you, like, you're just a patient person.

500
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:10,940
And you don't get to claim that, like, the fruit is, that the Spirit is producing this great patience in you while you're not loving or joyful or kind.

501
00:35:11,720 --> 00:35:13,680
Like, it's a holistic package.

502
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:18,180
Like, it's an explanation of who Jesus is.

503
00:35:18,180 --> 00:35:22,760
So you can't reject Jesus and then become like Jesus.

504
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:24,200
Does that make sense?

505
00:35:24,200 --> 00:35:27,820
Like, you can't say, I don't want to follow this guy.

506
00:35:27,820 --> 00:35:28,580
He's not my Lord.

507
00:35:28,580 --> 00:35:29,280
He's not my Savior.

508
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:30,260
I don't care about him.

509
00:35:30,260 --> 00:35:32,140
He's maybe a good teacher at best.

510
00:35:32,140 --> 00:35:35,300
And then naturally conform to the image of Jesus.

511
00:35:35,660 --> 00:35:59,120
And so, yes, like, unbelievers will be far more loving at times or joyful or kind, but the whole goal is to become like Jesus, which is why believers have this unique opportunity to allow God to create in them something that they have no ability to create outside of the work of Jesus in their life.

512
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:10,400
And so, if you're here and you're not a follower of Jesus, but this list sounds appealing to you, like you're like, this vision for life, I would love my life.

513
00:36:10,400 --> 00:36:20,300
And most of us in this room would probably say, I would love for my life to be built on the foundation of love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control.

514
00:36:20,380 --> 00:36:21,620
That sounds excellent.

515
00:36:21,620 --> 00:36:29,020
The reason that sounds excellent is because that is God's design for his humanity, and Jesus lived it out perfectly.

516
00:36:29,020 --> 00:36:37,180
And he has invited people to follow his example, to live out this characteristic perfectly.

517
00:36:37,180 --> 00:36:47,120
This is ultimately God's design, and this is what God is going to usher in his kingdom when he comes back and when he restores all things as they should be.

518
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:52,800
This character is the human expression of God's ultimate design.

519
00:36:52,800 --> 00:36:54,880
That's why we talk about abundant life.

520
00:36:54,880 --> 00:37:00,060
Like, this is what abundant life looks like, us living into the characteristics of Jesus.

521
00:37:00,060 --> 00:37:03,740
Because that's what we were designed to do.

522
00:37:03,740 --> 00:37:06,940
When I was a youth pastor, I used to play this game with the kids.

523
00:37:06,940 --> 00:37:11,100
And I would get some two-by-fours and some, like, long nails.

524
00:37:11,100 --> 00:37:12,620
Like, long nails.

525
00:37:13,260 --> 00:37:22,580
And I would give one kid a rock and one kid, like, a helmet and one kid, like, a pool noodle and another kid a hammer.

526
00:37:23,680 --> 00:37:27,180
And then I would make them race to see who could get the nail on the board the fastest.

527
00:37:27,180 --> 00:37:29,000
And guess who won every single time?

528
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:31,960
Thanks.

529
00:37:31,960 --> 00:37:33,060
Thanks.

530
00:37:33,060 --> 00:37:35,800
No, the kid with the hammer, they won every single time.

531
00:37:35,800 --> 00:37:42,780
Unless there was, like, a really, like, handyman kid with a rock, then sometimes he would beat the not-so-handy kid with a hammer.

532
00:37:42,860 --> 00:37:46,040
But the reason is because that's what the hammer is designed to do.

533
00:37:46,040 --> 00:37:50,440
And this is what humanity is designed to do by God.

534
00:37:50,440 --> 00:37:55,020
Before the fall, we are designed to perfectly produce this type of fruit.

535
00:37:55,020 --> 00:37:59,120
Love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control.

536
00:37:59,120 --> 00:38:05,200
That's why when we live into this characteristic, it's what Jesus describes as the abundant life.

537
00:38:05,200 --> 00:38:08,480
I love how Tim Mackey puts it.

538
00:38:09,380 --> 00:38:17,020
Tim Mackey says, the most Spirit-filled people that you know are the most fully human people that you know.

539
00:38:17,020 --> 00:38:22,640
The Spirit is trying to pull us into a fuller humanity.

540
00:38:22,640 --> 00:38:27,140
This is God's design for our life.

541
00:38:27,140 --> 00:38:38,360
To become like Jesus in His love and His joy and His peace and His patience and His kindness and goodness and faithfulness and gentleness and self-control.

542
00:38:39,380 --> 00:38:46,100
Now, again, this is a simple illustration.

543
00:38:46,100 --> 00:38:51,180
It will be really easy for me as a preacher to come up here and say, all right, makes sense, right?

544
00:38:51,180 --> 00:38:51,880
Now go do it.

545
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:56,540
Like, we should all just be perfect at this next week because it's a simple illustration.

546
00:38:56,540 --> 00:39:00,880
Paul has opened up our eyes to understand how this process works.

547
00:39:02,080 --> 00:39:06,300
But like I said earlier, it's a simple illustration.

548
00:39:06,300 --> 00:39:08,640
It gives us some clarity to the process.

549
00:39:08,640 --> 00:39:14,040
But it doesn't make the process, it's not a shortcut to the end goal.

550
00:39:14,040 --> 00:39:18,020
It's a lifelong process of exploration.

551
00:39:18,020 --> 00:39:24,440
It's a lifelong process of daily, weekly, monthly asking ourselves,

552
00:39:25,560 --> 00:39:31,540
Is my life a hospitable environment for the Holy Spirit to produce this kind of fruit?

553
00:39:31,540 --> 00:39:37,180
To daily, weekly, monthly ask ourselves,

554
00:39:37,180 --> 00:39:47,480
What attitudes and actions am I participating in that are not creating a hospitable environment for the Holy Spirit to produce fruit?

555
00:39:51,840 --> 00:39:53,560
How can I change?

556
00:39:53,560 --> 00:40:00,980
What can I add to my life that would create a hospitable environment for the Holy Spirit to produce fruit?

557
00:40:00,980 --> 00:40:09,300
This is a lifelong process, Paul says in verse 24, after he gives us the fruit of the Spirit.

558
00:40:09,300 --> 00:40:10,980
He says there's no law against these things.

559
00:40:11,040 --> 00:40:22,080
And he says those who belong to Christ have nailed their passions and desires of their sinful nature to Jesus' cross and crucified them there.

560
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:32,960
Since we are now living by the Spirit, let us follow the Spirit's leading in every part of our lives.

561
00:40:32,960 --> 00:40:39,120
Let us not become conceited or provoke one another or be jealous of one another.

562
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:43,860
Let the Holy Spirit lead us in every part of our lives.

563
00:40:43,860 --> 00:40:45,560
Do you hear that lifelong language?

564
00:40:45,560 --> 00:40:53,700
I was talking to a pastor who's been a pastor and a leader for like 40 years this week.

565
00:40:53,700 --> 00:41:00,580
And he said, you know, the more you walk with Jesus, the more you realize how much you aren't like him.

566
00:41:00,580 --> 00:41:03,760
This is a lifelong process.

567
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:15,120
The more time we spend with Jesus, the more we are aware of our sinfulness and our brokenness and our need for him to keep breaking through the soil and producing his character and his life in us.

568
00:41:18,220 --> 00:41:27,240
This is a helpful illustration and a lifelong tension of the believer.

569
00:41:29,020 --> 00:41:36,920
Our job now is to spend the rest of our lives creating a hospitable environment for God to produce his fruit.

570
00:41:36,920 --> 00:41:44,360
In our lives, we get to know Jesus who is the author, the beginning, and the perfecter, the end of our faith.

571
00:41:45,520 --> 00:41:51,100
And we get to know ourselves and the ways in which we naturally work against the Spirit in our life.

572
00:41:51,100 --> 00:41:57,680
This is the process that we've been invited into.

573
00:41:58,440 --> 00:42:01,620
And this is the vision of the Christian life.

574
00:42:01,620 --> 00:42:11,040
If you're here and you're not a follower of Jesus, sometimes the invitation to follow Jesus can be watered down or confused.

575
00:42:11,040 --> 00:42:13,440
Sometimes it's a pessimistic vision.

576
00:42:13,440 --> 00:42:15,920
I've heard people share the gospel and they're like, you're a sinner.

577
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,240
You're going to hell.

578
00:42:17,240 --> 00:42:20,780
Unless you just pray and repent right now and ask God for forgiveness.

579
00:42:20,780 --> 00:42:24,960
But the invitation of Jesus is so much more holistic and beautiful than that.

580
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:28,440
This invitation is, this is what I created you to be.

581
00:42:28,440 --> 00:42:31,320
You're a hammer and you're living your life like a pool noodle.

582
00:42:31,320 --> 00:42:33,240
I've created you to be a hammer.

583
00:42:33,240 --> 00:42:34,760
Now come into this image.

584
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:36,140
Come into this life.

585
00:42:36,140 --> 00:42:39,460
Live in the design that I have for you.

586
00:42:39,460 --> 00:42:43,600
So if you're living apart from that design,

587
00:42:43,600 --> 00:42:47,140
sometimes you're going to butt up against some things

588
00:42:47,140 --> 00:42:49,880
and you're going to not understand why life isn't fulfilling to you.

589
00:42:49,880 --> 00:42:51,840
It's because you're missing out.

590
00:42:53,040 --> 00:42:55,300
The invitation for you this morning is to come.

591
00:42:55,300 --> 00:43:00,300
To allow God to dwell in you.

592
00:43:00,300 --> 00:43:02,300
Show up in your life and plant a garden.

593
00:43:02,300 --> 00:43:08,620
And you just get to spend the rest of your life harvesting these fruits of the Spirit,

594
00:43:08,620 --> 00:43:11,400
this character of Jesus in your life.

595
00:43:11,400 --> 00:43:12,520
So for the rest of the series,

596
00:43:12,520 --> 00:43:16,640
we're going to look at each attribute, the character of Jesus.

597
00:43:16,640 --> 00:43:20,800
We're going to ask ourselves these three questions over and over again.

598
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:26,520
Is my life a hospitable environment for the Spirit to produce love or joy or patience?

599
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:34,600
What attitudes and actions are getting in the way of the Spirit producing love or joy or patience or kindness or goodness?

600
00:43:35,260 --> 00:43:44,180
What attitudes and actions can I add into my life that will create a hospitable environment for the Spirit to produce whatever fruit it is in our lives?

601
00:43:46,320 --> 00:43:56,480
My heart, my prayer for our church is that we would be individuals seeking to create an environment for the Holy Spirit to produce this type of fruit in our lives.

602
00:43:57,620 --> 00:44:12,600
Like I said at the beginning, I can't think of a better thing for our world in this time than believers of Jesus manifesting the character of Jesus in difficult situations,

603
00:44:12,600 --> 00:44:15,940
in complex, highly emotional political conversations.

604
00:44:19,560 --> 00:44:23,020
We do the same thing Jesus would do if He was in those situations.

605
00:44:23,020 --> 00:44:27,140
We ask ourselves daily, what would Jesus do if He were me?

606
00:44:27,140 --> 00:44:30,020
So I'm excited about this series.

607
00:44:30,020 --> 00:44:31,240
I hope you are too.

608
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:39,700
We're going to end this morning in one of the things that we do every single week as a church.

609
00:44:40,800 --> 00:44:47,940
And this is a thing that we do corporately to create a hospitable environment for the Spirit to produce the character of Jesus in our life.

610
00:44:47,940 --> 00:44:49,120
We take communion together.

611
00:44:49,120 --> 00:44:55,260
And communion is a reminder of both the crucifixion and the second coming.

612
00:44:55,260 --> 00:44:59,500
It's a reminder that we live in the tension between the two.

613
00:44:59,500 --> 00:45:07,900
And that our goal is to be conformed to the image of the Savior who His body was broken for us.

614
00:45:07,900 --> 00:45:10,160
His blood was shed for us.

615
00:45:10,200 --> 00:45:11,160
This is an opportunity.

616
00:45:11,160 --> 00:45:17,540
This is something we add into our lives to produce a hospitable environment for the Holy Spirit to work.

617
00:45:17,540 --> 00:45:29,200
And the crucifixion, His body broken, His blood shed, is the ultimate example of all of these characteristics lived out perfectly.

618
00:45:29,200 --> 00:45:32,800
Now, I think about two of them specifically this morning.

619
00:45:32,800 --> 00:45:39,660
The Scripture says, for the joy set before Jesus, He endured the cross.

620
00:45:40,100 --> 00:45:47,060
It was His joy that led Him to sacrificially lay down His life for us.

621
00:45:47,440 --> 00:45:56,680
Think about 1 John, that Jesus laid down His life for us.

622
00:45:56,680 --> 00:46:00,640
So we also ought to lay down our lives for our brothers and sisters.

623
00:46:00,780 --> 00:46:27,520
So this morning, I invite those of you that have placed your trust and allegiance in Jesus as the Lord of your life to take His body that was broken for you as a reminder of this character lived out on your behalf.

624
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:49,620
And we, again, we drink the juice as a reminder of what true love expressed looks like, of the invocation that we have to follow in that love.

625
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:52,700
Let's drink this juice together.

626
00:46:52,700 --> 00:47:10,500
Church, I'm looking forward to the opportunity to grow with you this summer into the image of Jesus.

627
00:47:10,500 --> 00:47:11,540
Let's take this seriously.

628
00:47:11,720 --> 00:47:18,440
Let's be intentional about allowing God to create these things in our lives.

629
00:47:18,440 --> 00:47:27,780
Let's be in relationship with one another so that when we live opposite this, we have brothers and sisters who love us enough to point it out.

630
00:47:27,780 --> 00:47:31,880
Let's encourage one another to become more like Jesus.

631
00:47:32,060 --> 00:47:42,580
There's nothing the city of Winchester needs now more than followers of Jesus becoming like Christ and engaging culture with this fruit.

632
00:47:42,580 --> 00:47:49,420
Love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, and self-control.

633
00:47:49,420 --> 00:47:49,940
Let's pray.

634
00:47:49,940 --> 00:47:52,500
Father, you are good.

635
00:47:57,840 --> 00:48:01,640
And against your character, there is no law.

636
00:48:01,640 --> 00:48:06,440
Perfect justice, perfect love, perfect faithfulness is found in you.

637
00:48:06,440 --> 00:48:12,200
God, may we be a people that allow you to manifest that in us.

638
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:17,300
Holy Spirit, show us when we get in the way of that process.

639
00:48:17,300 --> 00:48:20,440
Show us when we're neglecting that process.

640
00:48:22,240 --> 00:48:24,060
Draw us back into the invitation.

641
00:48:24,060 --> 00:48:27,880
Not out of shame.

642
00:48:27,880 --> 00:48:34,720
But out of an invitation to live in the way in which you designed us to live.

643
00:48:34,720 --> 00:48:35,540
For your glory.

644
00:48:35,540 --> 00:48:36,780
For our good.

645
00:48:36,780 --> 00:48:38,580
In Jesus' name I pray.

646
00:48:38,580 --> 00:48:39,600
Amen.

647
00:48:39,600 --> 00:48:44,200
Alright church, thanks for hanging out with us this morning.

648
00:48:44,200 --> 00:48:45,560
Hang out with your friends.
